{"title":"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems/A1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> denote the set of all ordered triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/4876a849f749382efc62de5e1d6867977392af5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> of nonnegative integers. Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c7e0ab403e3d15a101a2f2cdd807508a0ac6839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:T \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> such that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d4e8080418f5bb567971c0ee129fd02c7c7b13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p,q,r) = \\begin{cases} 0 &amp; \\text{if} \\; pqr = 0, \\\\ 1 + \\tfrac{1}{6}\\{f(p + 1,q - 1,r) + f(p - 1,q + 1,r) &amp; \\\\ + f(p - 1,q,r + 1) + f(p + 1,q,r - 1) &amp; \\\\ + f(p,q + 1,r - 1) + f(p,q - 1,r + 1)\\} &amp; \\text{otherwise.} \\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -43px\" width=\"537\" height=\"96\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855e162fe1d412f57eb4c63831798db4f031355e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(p,q,r)=\\frac{3pqr}{p+q+r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"165\" height=\"41\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd129b585f3197eb8aaf364f7b0840a0b5801143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr\\neq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4aed08012d304c6a82190e129bf6d83a07af0c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(p,q,r)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a013a6e428370221360f9987a7b64a86f30c529b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> satisfies the equation. Suppose there exists another solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/31068115b4a66cea3050eaf0556e94ded5fc81f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p,q,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13d81e3014b1278a95f61bc35e569f0a82371df1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(p,q,r)=f(p,q,r)-h(p,q,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"246\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd383a94fffab1b62955c11a54106da410c6e12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f=g+h,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> satisfies the relationship <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b9893fb37eea17c85555c47ecdb489c1ef0831d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(p,q,r)=\\begin{cases} \\tfrac{1}{6}\\{g(p + 1,q - 1,r) + g(p - 1,q + 1,r) &amp; \\\\ + g(p - 1,q,r + 1) + g(p + 1,q,r - 1) &amp; \\\\ + g(p,q + 1,r - 1) + g(p,q - 1,r + 1)\\}\\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -33px\" width=\"408\" height=\"75\" />, so that each value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to 6 points around it with an equal sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08ff3681d6992f69ee41e21c7237c89f970ac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />. This implies that for fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08ff3681d6992f69ee41e21c7237c89f970ac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03ca01ecbfa0db5828eab722ef01ce6b111dd5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(p,q,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> is constant. Furthermore, some values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are always zero; for example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e7fdfa76bfd40dc79d4319955c7be0f607e572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p,2,0)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> by the problem statement, and similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21de8d0b93e2aa89942bc5fcd9efacbbbfe8c932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(p,2,0)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24dab321cf8b837b2b2c28d8eddf779000bc077a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(p,2,0)=0-0=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be identically zero, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the only function satisfying this equation.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2001 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=17447\">Discussion on AOPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185724\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 123/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4524/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7170:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017185724 and revision id 32371. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}